{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/98540-cwod-pod-of-more-older-books","id":98540,"title":"cWoD PoD of more older books....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T12:03:04-07:00","id":98540,"title":"cWoD PoD of more older books....","content":"M20 has now added a PoD of Penny Dreadful as a Stretch Goal. While commenting on that, and the fact, that I like the book, but not like that it's PoD is now tied to M20s funding.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of other concepts on how to make money, so the initial costs of the recreation of print files could be raised....<br /> <br /> <br /> And I was thinking this could work:<br /> <br /> Start a poll of all books, that aren't in PoD yet.<br /> <br /> Every month start a &quot;fundraising week&quot; at DriveThru, where the PDF price of that book is raised for 7 days.<br /> <br /> If the extra funds are enough to have the PoD files created, good, and all those who bought in those 7 days should get a coupon for the PoD at cost once it is finished, so that they have paied the same as a PDF/PoD combo would normally cost.<br /> <br /> If the extra fundes aren't enough, give the additional money spend back, as a bonus to the DriveThru account.<br /> <br /> That way, the system is like a kickstarter, without actually using a kickstarter for every single book.<br /> Changing the price of a PDF within DriveThru shouldn't be that difficult, there are sales all the time.<br /> Keeping track of the extra money earned, shouldn't be that difficult either. Drivethru has to pay OOP/CCP for the books sold anyway.<br /> Refunding, if it doesn't work, shouldn't be that difficult either.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> Would you pay more for a PDF now, if you know that you can get the PoD later - and come out with more or less the same price as PDF/PoD would cost later, anyway ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T13:13:21-07:00","id":98596,"title":"","content":"I would definitely support that idea. There are a bunch that I would love to get in print that I can't yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T15:50:07-07:00","id":98726,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure it is as practically easy as it sounds.<br /> <br /> It also puts a fairly large arbitrary cap on which older books are going to stand a chance and which ones don't. There are some older books in the back log that could probably get pushed through with a bit of extra funding. There are others that are much more work than one week of slightly higher prices is going to accomplish. From a psychological perspective it seems like it wouldn't be that popular (And therefore wouldn't raise all that much money for the task at hand).<br /> <br /> This actually seems to me something that Onyx Path could to to break up their new book Kickstarters a bit. I've seen plenty of people stress over the, essentially, 1/month Kickstarters and the hit on the wallet the deluxe editions represent. Having an occasional Kickstarter to fund the preparation of high quality PDF and POD files for the backlog seems a much better structured way to accomplish this, and probably would be much lower key Kickstarter drives since there isn't nearly as much overhead that needs to be addressed. As well, there isn't new material to worry about; stretch goals can focus on adding some shorter books to the list of ones the money will pay for getting dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T17:29:53-07:00","id":98811,"title":"","content":"The Penny Dreadful fiction is probably mostly just text. Unlike other books, it can be re-created pretty easily once the copy (words) are recreated. There isn't much in the way of lay-out and illustration work to re-scan, re-discover, and make into a usable document.<br /> <br /> Just about every other book requires scanning pages, cleaning them up, and correcting the tones so that it looks good, or the files have to be found/fixed/corrected so that an &quot;original electronic&quot; file can be produced. I think the books that have been released already on PoD were the &quot;low hanging fruit&quot; (complete files, or easy-to-recreate ones that didn't require too much work.) The rest are more-or-less apparently happening as they can be re-scanned and made available, but it's taking more time and effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T01:51:08-07:00","id":99025,"title":"","content":"The &quot;words&quot; of Penny Dreadfull are present. I already told Matt, in the old forums, that it took me all about 30 miinutes to locate the files with the wayback machine and download an open source program that can strip PDFs for background images, and other art as well as text. But, the quality wouldn't be good enough to be printed, said Matt. Well, so someone has to recreate the art, high res, I suppose.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking kickstarter before, but I couldn't figure out a good measure of rewart tiers. A printed book would be nice, a PoD coupon would not be so nice, since you fund the Kickstarter and still have to pay (a reduced) cost for the book. PDF would be nice, but just like &quot;Screaming Path&quot; for M20 it is pointless if you already own it...<br /> So, giving the backers DriveThru Gift Cards, so they can buy PDFs or PoD as they see fit (and grant coupons to those who bought the PDF before). Sounds nice, but one would need other incentives too. For &quot;Back for $20 to get a $15 Gift Card&quot; doesn't seem that clever, even for a fundraising campaign....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T07:09:14-07:00","id":99136,"title":"","content":"So, since I already had a database full of all cWoD books, and whether or not they are PoD, I coded a poll....<br /> <br /> It's totally unofficial and certainly not hacker proofed, bot proofed, but besides that it allows to generate an overview on what books people might want to see as PoD more badly than others...<br /> <br /> Check out: <a href=\"http://www.werwolf-live.de/book_wishlist.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.werwolf-live.de/book_wishlist.php</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T06:39:59-07:00","id":99968,"title":"","content":"Oh, feel free to use the poll and post feedback...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T04:18:57-07:00","id":102543,"title":"","content":"okay, seems like not so many people are interested in sharing, what books they'd like to enter PoD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T06:16:27-07:00","id":102583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/98540-cwod-pod-of-more-older-books?p=102543#post102543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">okay, seems like not so many people are interested in sharing, what books they'd like to enter PoD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that a lot people have a few but most aren't interested enough to post their favourites.<br /> <br /> I'd personally like to see the 1st edition core books as PDF since they're really hard to find. Not that I'm really interested in playing by 1st edit rules but I like reading through the older editions and see how and why rules and settings have evolved over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T07:38:35-07:00","id":102616,"title":"","content":"Current format is very time consuming (that's why I've only filled in a dozen or so). Any chance of a search or suggestion based method?<br /> <br /> Duplicate collections should probably be cleaned up. For example, 1st ed Tribe books are represented by themselves and by Litany of the Tribes at the moment.<br /> <br /> Also, Secrets of Elysium should probably be removed - that was released as Laws of Elysium which is available as PoD already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 03-31-2014, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T03:06:43-07:00","id":103277,"title":"","content":"Do you know any framework to create such a search ?<br /> If not, the Search already implemented in the browser works. It's usually Cntrl+F.<br /> <br /> I might add that to the description above...<br /> <br /> I thought about removing those books, that are in compilations, but I figured that some people might want the single book, instead of the compilation. Same is true for &quot;Secrets of the Elysium&quot;. It appears on the official listing of all books twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T05:16:16-07:00","id":103312,"title":"","content":"A little outside my area of expertise but something like <a href=\"http://julesjanssen.github.io/chosen/\" target=\"_blank\">http://julesjanssen.github.io/chosen/</a> might do the trick.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm suggesting these kinds of simplifications is that the current setup is very unfriendly to casual answering - there's a substantial hump of effort that has to be put in by the answerer which won't be invested by anyone who is not that pushed about ranking future PoD outputs.<br /> <br /> As the majority of high desire books are already in PoD at this stage, you want to make it as easy as possible for people to select the one or two &quot;personal favourites&quot; they might be missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 04-01-2014, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T09:22:28-07:00","id":103437,"title":"","content":"Ok. I have added a select, but the updating depending on the search term doesn't yet. I have to check for that another time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T23:04:00-07:00","id":103863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/98540-cwod-pod-of-more-older-books?p=102543#post102543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">okay, seems like not so many people are interested in sharing, what books they'd like to enter PoD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd like the following:<br /> - Clanbook Salubri;<br /> - Clanbook Cappadocian;<br /> - the Libellus Sanguinis books;<br /> - Ashen Thief;<br /> - Ashen Knight;<br /> - Ashen Cults;<br /> - Cainite Heresy; and<br /> - Transylvania by Night.<br /> <br /> However, I'm a realist. Most old, scanned, products lack original production files (necessary for OEF, I guess), or lack intact files.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T02:28:51-07:00","id":103926,"title":"","content":"you are invited to add them on the page, too.<br /> Even if you currently have to pick them out of the list manually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T06:58:40-07:00","id":104012,"title":"","content":"Now the searchbox works, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T10:42:44-07:00","id":117994,"title":"","content":"With &quot;<a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=188&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Liege, Lord and Lackey</a>&quot; and &quot;<a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=41&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Crafts</a>&quot; two books entered the PoD, that <a href=\"http://www.werwolf-live.de/book_wishlist.php\" target=\"_blank\">were wished for</a> - not that that would be the reason with only three participants having voted one can't really say which books fans would really want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T04:09:15-07:00","id":273595,"title":"","content":"The last post here is 6 months old and the last older books that went into PoD were <i><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=98228&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Penny Dreadful</a></i> and <i><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=127744&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Truth Until Paradox revised</a></i> (if it is the same as 2nd Edition, I don't know).<br /> <br /> So, I was wondering why is that?<br /> Is there no market for the older books?<br /> Is it just taking longer to get printable files reproduced?<br /> Is there someone working on them or not ?<br /> <br /> I has been a while since I created a <a href=\"http://werwolf-live.de/book_wishlist.php\" target=\"_blank\">web-interface</a> where people can indicate which books they would love to see as PoD, but beside myself only two people ever went there. And all of us agreed on <i><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=2292&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">London by Night</a></i> as &quot;must be PoD&quot;. Meanwhile the books I'd like to get my hands on to complete my collection are still having astronomical prices on amazon marketplace.<br /> <br /> Where the kickstarter to <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Mage20</a> brought us Penny, I hope the VDA20 Kickstarter will also not only create new content as a stretch goal, but also help to bring more of the back catalogue. Especially <i><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product_info.php?products_id=539&amp;affiliate_id=171789\" target=\"_blank\">Witches and Pagans</a></i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I'm curious, am I the only one, or are there more people here in the forums who which for more old stuff in PoD?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T08:45:33-07:00","id":277272,"title":"","content":"Personally I would love the chance to get Witches and Pagans as a PoD as well as Shadow Court for CtD just to name the two of the most obvious. I would think there being a market for the older books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}